= Meta pages =

Pages in the '''BITwiki:''' namespace document the BITwiki project itself rather than the external subject matter of the encyclopedia.

They include public architecture, governance, manifestos, schemas, migration notes, naming conventions, quality standards, deployment guidance, extension/capability documentation, and other public project knowledge.

== Identification rule ==
A page in the BITwiki namespace is meta unless it explicitly states otherwise. Canonical meta pages should also use {{tl|BITwiki meta}} so their status is visible in the rendered page and they are automatically categorized in [[:Category:BITwiki meta]].

== Ordinary knowledge ==
Subject-matter knowledge belongs in Main or another purpose-built content namespace. Meta documentation should not be mixed into encyclopedia articles merely because it discusses concepts such as ontology, epistemics, or systems theory.

